cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "allmeta — open browser-only tools for evidence synthesis"
message: >
  If you use allmeta in your research, please cite it using the metadata in this
  file. The `identifiers` block below carries the Zenodo concept DOI, which is
  version-less and always resolves to the latest archived release.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ahmad
    given-names: Mahmood
    # orcid: add your ORCID here (e.g. https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000)
repository-code: "https://github.com/mahmood726-cyber/allmeta"
url: "https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/allmeta/"
# Concept DOI — version-less, always resolves to the latest archived release.
# The v1.0.0 per-release DOI is 10.5281/zenodo.20516881.
identifiers:
  - description: "Zenodo concept DOI (all versions)"
    type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.20516880"
abstract: >
  allmeta is a browser-only catalog of evidence-synthesis tools spanning
  pairwise and network meta-analysis, diagnostic test accuracy, dose-response
  modelling, risk-of-bias assessment, GRADE, PRISMA, trial sequential analysis,
  individual participant data analysis, and clinical decision support. Each app
  is a self-contained HTML+JS+CSS bundle that runs offline; computation happens
  client-side and no data is uploaded. Many numerical engines are cross-checked
  against canonical R packages (metafor, meta, netmeta, mada). Selected apps
  emit HMAC-signed TruthCert receipts so reviewers can verify that the inputs
  and outputs in a result page match the analysis that produced them.
keywords:
  - meta-analysis
  - systematic-review
  - network-meta-analysis
  - diagnostic-test-accuracy
  - risk-of-bias
  - grade
  - prisma
  - trial-sequential-analysis
  - evidence-synthesis
  - reproducibility
  - browser-only
  - webr
